# Large data / model artifacts — never commit these
*.parquet
*.npy
*.keras
*.pkl
*.h5
data_v4/
data_v5/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
# .vscode/ is tracked on purpose: tasks.json + settings.json are the Cursor workflow

# site/serving/ IS committed — Render has no access to data_v5/, so the
# deployed app can only read what is in the repo. The bundle is small
# (single-digit MB: pruned matchups, per-player priors, exported weights)
# and build_serving_artifacts.py refuses to write one over BUNDLE_MAX_MB.
# The blanket bans above still apply everywhere else, so re-allow the
# specific extensions inside it. Rebuild it after EVERY retrain.
!site/serving/
!site/serving/**
site/serving/*.pkl
